SUMMARY:Community Celebration of the Reading of the Declaration of Independence
DESCRIPTION:What better way to commemorate this historic date than by having local Montclair students read aloud the famous words that have inspired abolitionists\, suffragists\, civil rights leaders\, labor organizers and countless others to fight to extend liberty and equality more fully than at our nation’s founding. The program will also include a talk by Steve Golin\, professor emeritus of Bloomfield College\, on why its significance lies not only in what it achieved in 1776\, but in how its words have continued to challenge every generation to live up to them. Kick start your July 4th plans by sharing in an uplifting and patriotic party! \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/community-celebration-of-the-reading-of-the-declaration-of-independence/
