SUMMARY:15 th Annual Taubman Piano Festival
DESCRIPTION:Montclair State University’s Cali School of Music presents the 15th Annual Taubman Piano Festival on June 27–28\, 2026. The festival features two public piano recitals\, with admission available at the door for $20. \nSaturday\, June 27 at 4:00 p.m.\nEsteban Castro \nPianist and composer Esteban Castro has performed internationally at leading venues and festivals including the Montreux Jazz Festival\, The Blue Note\, Birdland\, and NPR Tiny Desk. A full-scholarship student at The Juilliard School and a private student of Fred Hersch\, Castro became the youngest-ever winner of the Montreux Jazz Piano Solo Competition at age 13. \nHis recital will feature a variety of compositions and original improvisations. \nSunday\, June 28 at 4:00 p.m.\nFei-Fei \nAcclaimed for her poetic artistry and charismatic stage presence\, pianist Fei-Fei is a winner of the Concert Artists Guild Competition and a top finalist at the 14th Van Cliburn International Piano Competition. She has performed worldwide as a soloist and recitalist\, including appearances at Carnegie Hall and with major orchestras across the United States\, Europe\, Asia\, and Central America. \nHer recital will include works by Beethoven\, Rachmaninoff\, and Chopin. \nFor details\, contact Dr. David Witten at wittend@montclair.edu. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/15-th-annual-taubman-paino-festival/2026-06-28/
LOCATION:Leshowitz Hall\, Montclair State University\, 1 Normal Avenue\, Montclair\, NJ\, 07043\, United States
CATEGORIES:Live Music
